From 07538210e6f204a70a4d9ae424914608a32f9c69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UZDoom NX2 <uzdoom-nx2@users.noreply.local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:01:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 71/71] Switch 2 0.1.2: console, rumble, gyro aiming, GPU hang
 handling

- Console: A (Switch keyboard) now runs the command. The pad buttons that
  stand for keys were converted to a key event that was then dropped. B
  closes the console.
- Rumble (nx2_motion.cpp): devkitPro's SDL2 never set up the vibration of
  its first joystick and sent out-of-range values; I_Rumble now drives the
  HID vibration devices of the active controller directly.
- Gyro aiming (nx2_motion.cpp): six-axis sensors of the active controller,
  player-space yaw (follows gravity), nx_gyro, nx_gyro_sensitivity,
  nx_gyro_invert_x/_y, nx_gyro_deadzone; gyro_reset (left stick click when
  free) levels the view.
- No ZCULL on the scene depth again (rd_vk_zcull 0, as in 0.1.0): the first
  3D frame of Freedoom: Phase 1 hung with OunceVK 20261118's new ZCULL.
- GPU waits are bounded (20 s): a hung GPU stops the game with an error
  instead of freezing it; the hang watchdog now follows Vulkan frames and
  the engine's own thread, and writes hang.log.
- SD firewall: mkdir of an existing folder above the sandbox ("/switch")
  answers EEXIST without writing (OunceVK's mkdir -p of its cache).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
